{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6EpGac7ebshsr3Q3vDCmN","type":"tool_result","content":"The release notes mention both changes under **Breaking Changes**, but they don't explain the behavior:\n\n- For `toHaveTextContent`: \"`toHaveTextContent` is strict, add `toMatchTextContent` as alternative\" (PR #10473, by @sheremet-va). So the existing matcher now applies stricter matching, and `toMatchTextContent` is offered as a looser option.\n- For locators in browser mode: \"Enable `locators.exact` by default\" (PR #10430, by @sheremet-va). Locator text matching now defaults to exact matching.\n\nThe page doesn't define what \"strict\" or \"exact\" mean here, so check the Vitest docs or the linked PRs for the details."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9201ce1f-0e01-4f5a-b238-37bb1aab7549","uuid":"623738f7-f1b2-4994-b706-edb1430fa3b7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:21.639Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":451736,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The release notes mention both changes under **Breaking Changes**, but they don't explain the behavior:\n\n- For `toHaveTextContent`: \"`toHaveTextContent` is strict, add `toMatchTextContent` as alternative\" (PR #10473, by @sheremet-va). So the existing matcher now applies stricter matching, and `toMatchTextContent` is offered as a looser option.\n- For locators in browser mode: \"Enable `locators.exact` by default\" (PR #10430, by @sheremet-va). Locator text matching now defaults to exact matching.\n\nThe page doesn't define what \"strict\" or \"exact\" mean here, so check the Vitest docs or the linked PRs for the details.","durationMs":5232,"url":"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G6EpGac7ebshsr3Q3vDCmN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
