{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnT353U1UwLwQm83qcx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Vitest 5, use `toMatchTextContent` for a partial match: `await expect.element(page.getByTestId('msg')).toMatchTextContent('your phrase')`. `toHaveTextContent` is strict now, so it only passes when the text matches exactly. Locators also match text exactly by default in Vitest 5 (`locators.exact` is `true`), so to find the element by part of its text, pass `{ exact: false }`, as in `page.getByText('your phrase', { exact: false })`. On Vitest 4 or earlier, `toHaveTextContent('your phrase')` already does a partial match.\n\nThe v5.0.0 release notes list both changes, but they don't define \"strict\" exactly. If it matters, for example whitespace handling, check the matcher docs.\n\nSources:\n- [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":5394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9201ce1f-0e01-4f5a-b238-37bb1aab7549","uuid":"da4b170e-4010-4a94-a274-4107f5793ba1","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:26.022Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnT2ov8ZsbUXEH1PDpi"}
